--- !u!114 &1709852092
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1709852081}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 40fe67fde4a4351409089804b4848b92, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  _documentationText: 'Image Classification MobileNet Example

    Classifies each
    input frame with a MobileNetV2 ImageNet model using OpenCV DNN or Unity Sentis.

    

    Demonstrates:

    -
    Reading input frames via MultiSourceToMatHelper (webcam, video file, image file,
    or GPU readback)

    - Loading MobileNet ONNX/Sentis model from StreamingAssets
    and embedded ImageNet labels (Imagenet1kLabels)

    - Preprocessing with Image2BlobParams
    and blobFromImageWithParams (opencv_zoo demo.cpp)

    - Toggling Sentis vs
    OpenCV DNN inference and optional async classification

    - Converting RGBA
    frames to RGB and reading top class from output Mat

    

    OpenCV classes
    and APIs used:

    - Mat, Size, Scalar, Image2BlobParams

    - Core: minMaxLoc,
    subtract, multiply, split, merge

    - Imgproc: cvtColor, resize

    - MultiBackendNet,
    MatSingleFlightSyncAsyncRunner, MultiBackendDnn

    - MultiSourceToMatHelper,
    OpenCVMatUnityUtils

    

    Referring to:

    https://github.com/opencv/opencv_zoo/tree/master/models/image_classification_mobilenet

    

    [Tested
    Models]

    https://github.com/opencv/opencv_zoo/raw/6c59fd8aaedf1728138e3c982f3351bf9ee3013a/models/image_classification_mobilenet/image_classification_mobilenetv2_2022apr.onnx'
  AlignmentSetting: 0
